{"step_index":340,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:35:05Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-07T07:35:05+01:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-07T07:35:05+01:00\nShowing lines 101-163 of 163\n101: python cli_scanner.py --rules\n102: \n103: # 5. Whitelist (allow) a trusted process\n104: python cli_scanner.py --allow internal_admin.exe\n105: \n106: # 6. Blacklist (ban) a malicious process or remote IP\n107: python cli_scanner.py --block bad_tool.exe\n108: python cli_scanner.py --block 198.51.100.50\n109: \n110: # 7. Generate and send full HTML security report to email\n111: python cli_scanner.py --email-report admin@yourdomain.com\n112: \n113: # 8. Check specifically for Remote Desktop / RMM / VNC sessions\n114: python cli_scanner.py --rmm\n115: \n116: # 9. Forcefully terminate a specific PID or entire process tree\n117: python cli_scanner.py --kill-pid 1234\n118: python cli_scanner.py --kill-tree 1234\n119: ```\n120: \n121: ---\n122: \n123: ## 📁 File Structure\n124: \n125: ```\n126: SpywareProcessMon/\n127: ├── backend/\n128: │   ├── __init__.py\n129: │   ├── config.py              # Configuration, whitelists, critical binaries, ports\n130: │   ├── policy_engine.py       # Allowlist, blocklist & Windows Firewall rules engine\n131: │   ├── network_tracer.py      # Network process auditor, reverse DNS, GeoIP & Genuineness scorer\n132: │   ├── email_notifier.py      # SMTP dispatcher & HTML threat report generator\n133: │   ├── signatures_db.py       # Catalog of LOLRMM tools, RATs, infostealers, heuristics\n134: │   ├── pe_analyzer.py         # Pure-Python PE parser, Shannon entropy, API string scanner\n135: │   ├── network_monitor.py     # Sockets, listening ports, remote connections, RMM ports\n136: │   ├── persistence_hunter.py  # Startup folders, Registry Run keys, Scheduled Tasks\n137: │   ├── detector.py            # Multi-vector detection engine (8 analysis passes)\n138: │   ├── remediator.py          # Kill engine, process tree terminator, quarantine, audit log\n139: │   ├── simulator.py           # Benign threat simulation test suite\n140: │   └── server.py              # FastAPI REST API + WebSockets telemetry server\n141: ├── database/\n142: │   ├── policy_rules.json      # Persistent whitelist and blacklist rules\n143: │   ├── email_config.json      # SMTP server configuration\n144: │   └── geo_cache.json         # Cached IP intelligence lookups\n145: ├── frontend/\n146: │   ├── index.html             # Cyber SOC Dashboard UI\n147: │   ├── css/\n148: │   │   └── dashboard.css      # Dark SOC cyber styling, animations, glow effects\n149: │   └── js/\n150: │       └── app.js             # Real-time WebSocket/polling, state management, audio chimes\n151: ├── cli_scanner.py             # CLI tool for terminal scans, kills, and network tracing\n152: ├── run_server.py              # Server launcher script with automatic browser open\n153: ├── start_dashboard.bat        # Windows 1-click batch launcher\n154: ├── requirements.txt           # Python dependencies (fastapi, uvicorn, psutil, requests)\n155: └── README.md                  # Complete documentation\n156: ```\n157: \n158: ---\n159: \n160: ## 🔒 Security & Safety Controls\n161: 1. **Critical System Whitelist:** Protected system processes (`system`, `registry`, `smss.exe`, `csrss.exe`, `wininit.exe`, `services.exe`, `lsass.exe`) running from verified `System32` paths cannot be terminated.\n162: 2. **Access Control Overrides:** Whitelisted software cannot be flagged or terminated by automated scans.\n163: 3. **Audit Trail:** Every scan, process termination, tree kill, quarantine, and email dispatch is logged in `logs/audit_events.json` and exportable as JSON."}
